<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Release entitlements, referenced by tauri.conf.json > bundle > macOS >
      entitlements. Kept separate from Entitlements.plist because that file
      carries the Xcode-only $(AppIdentifierPrefix) token, which `codesign`
      does not expand — scripts/build-signed-app.sh resolves it at sign time,
      but tauri-bundler hands the file to codesign verbatim, so the team
      prefix has to be literal here.

      The Team ID is public information (it appears in the signature of every
      shipped build), so committing it is not a secret leak.

      Required for biometric (Touch ID) unlock: commands/keychain.rs stores the
      os_kek as a generic password guarded by a SecAccessControl with
      BIOMETRY_CURRENT_SET, and macOS refuses that without this entitlement.

      This entitlement is provisioning-profile restricted. A bundle declaring
      it is killed at spawn unless Contents/embedded.provisionprofile holds a
      *Developer ID* profile covering the access group — see
      docs/plans/2026-09-14-release-v0.1.0/phase-0-signing-spike.md for the
      isolated experiment table. The profile is supplied via
      bundle.macOS.files, which the bundler copies in before codesign runs.
    -->
    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>86H6CNLN4C.app.memlore</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
